# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=shaman:restoration style=flee size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=carried (behaves as fresh, #273).
# carried/fresh only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
# unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing out to a real
# RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26 driver-lesson recipe),
# rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight "visiting" framing.
#
# Checked against sessions.jsonl and direction.md first: `flee` has appeared
# in exactly two evenings before (priest:discipline and druid:guardian, both
# 10-normal, both stalled in THE VIGIL as part of [[#6]]'s convergence
# evidence) and never at 25-heroic, and never on a healer spec. [[#6]] already
# has two styles (good, dodge) that stalled at 10-normal but crossed THE
# VIGIL clean at 25-heroic, with an open question of whether size/difficulty
# is the real axis rather than style -- this is the first chance to test that
# with a style that has already shown the 10-normal stall shape twice. It is
# also a healer, so a clean or stalled crossing here also feeds [[#1]] and
# [[#7]]'s question of what a body that only flees costs a raid, this time
# across a whole evening rather than one pull.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:shaman:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening flee 260 5
state
shot end
says
bill
